{"answerArea":{"calculator":false,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"$\\displaystyle\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}\\left| \\,\\frac{{{a}_{n+1}}}{{{a}_{n}}}\\, \\right|=\\dfrac{5}{8}$\n\n[[☃ explanation 1]]","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{"explanation 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"explanation":"$\\begin{align}\n\u0026\\phantom{=}\\displaystyle\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}\\left| \\,\\frac{{{a}_{n+1}}}{{{a}_{n}}}\\, \\right|\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\displaystyle\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}\\left| \\dfrac{(-5)^{n+1}}{(n+4)8^{n+2}} \\cdot \\dfrac{(n+3)8^{n+1}}{(-5)^n} \\right|\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\displaystyle\\lim_{n\\to\\infty} \\left| \\dfrac{-5(n+3)}{(n+4)8} \\right|\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{5}{8}\n\\end{align}$","hidePrompt":"Got it, thanks!","showPrompt":"Show entire process.","static":false,"widgets":{}},"static":false,"type":"explanation","version":{"major":0,"minor":0}}}},{"content":"Since the limit, $\\dfrac{5}{8}$, is less than $1$, the ratio test tells us that the series converges.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"$a_n=\\dfrac{(-5)^n}{(n+3)8^{n+1}}$\n\n**1) Find $\\displaystyle\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}\\left| \\dfrac{a_{n+1}}{a_n} \\right|$.**\n\n$\\displaystyle\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}\\left|\\, \\frac{{{a}_{n+1}}}{{{a}_{n}}} \\,\\right|=$ [[☃ input-number 1]]\n\n**2) Based on your answer, what does the ratio test say about $S=\\displaystyle\\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty}a_n$?**\n\n[[☃ radio 1]]","images":{},"widgets":{"input-number 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"answerType":"number","inexact":false,"maxError":0.1,"simplify":"required","size":"normal","value":0.625},"static":false,"type":"input-number","version":{"major":0,"minor":0}},"radio 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"choices":[{"content":"The series converges.","correct":true},{"content":"The series diverges.","correct":false},{"content":"The test is inc